<title>AUSTRALIA: Minproc appoints new executives.</title>
<headline>Minproc appoints new executives.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Contract miner Minproc Engineers Ltd said on Tuesday it had appointed Kevin Wealand managing director and Michael Spratt chief operating officer.</p>
<p>This follows the resignation on May 22 of former chief executive, Peter Anderton.</p>
<p>Minproc said Wealand was previously a senior executive in Mobil Australia and managing director of Swan Brewery before operating a consultancy business.</p>
<p>Spratt was previously managing director of silicon producer, Simcoa, having had extensive experience in the minerals industries.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
